00:13:55,201 --> 00:13:57,860
it says they're Hideyoshi's comrades who are making their mark,
doesn't it?

260
00:13:58,360 --> 00:14:00,540
Japanese history is
going to be a total mess.

261
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:02,720
This has become a serious problem,
hasn't it?

262
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,820
Ryotsu-dono, thank you so much.

263
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,320
I don't know how to thank you.

264
00:14:10,460 --> 00:14:12,780
So don't forget,
half of the fortune is mine.

265
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:14,400
Yes, yes, I know.

266
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:15,460
You promised!

267
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:19,320
Next time,
it really will be Osaka Castle, right?

268
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:25,340
Over one mountain, bookshelves and all,
off to Osaka Castle, go!

269
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:30,540
What is this place?

270
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,680
Isn't this the same as last time, senpai?

271
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:35,840
That's strange.

272
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:38,000
It's you lot again? What are you doing?

273
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:41,120
Hey, where's Osaka Castle?
Where's Hideyoshi?

274
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:43,760
I keep telling you,
I don't know any such guy!

275
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:47,240
He's supposed to have unified the country!

276
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,247
What are you talking about, you two?

277
00:14:50,297 --> 00:14:52,620
It was Lord Oda Nobunaga
who took control of the realm.

278
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:53,260
Whoa!

279
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:53,880
Hehehe!

280
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:57,760
Nobunaga was killed by Akechi Mitsuhide at Honnō-ji,
you know!

281
00:14:58,020 --> 00:15:00,308
What a ridiculous story.

282
00:15:00,358 --> 00:15:04,700
Lord Nobunaga is still alive and well,
and he's the ruler of the realm!

283
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:07,500
What's going on, Honda!

284
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:10,080
I-I don't know anything about that!

285
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,780
Well, there's no helping it. Let's go back.

286
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:13,740
Again?

287
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,360
What should I do?

288
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:20,880
Should I blame him?

289
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,680
Maybe I should just drop it.

290
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:24,020
So?

291
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:26,140
Why are you hesitating now,
after coming this far?

292
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:27,240
Easier said than done.

293
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:29,460
What should I do?

294
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:30,840
Should I blame him?

295
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,820
I think I'll drop it after all.

296
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:35,040
I think I'll blame him after all.

297
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:41,500
"If it won't sing, kill it,"

298
00:15:45,460 --> 00:15:45,900
Whoa!

299
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,520
Lord Nobunaga!

300
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:50,700
It's Hideyoshi!

301
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:53,940
You're supposed to be
attacking Takamatsu Castle!

302
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,520
Why are you here?

303
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:58,940
That's well, no questions asked!

304
00:15:59,040 --> 00:15:59,620
Gaah!

305
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:01,300
Yay!

306
00:16:02,140 --> 00:16:02,880
Yay!

307
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:06,540
Yay!

308
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:07,120
Yay!

309
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:07,900
Yay!

310
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:09,580
Yay!

311
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:45,660
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee...
Yeah, yeah, good, good, good, good, good, good!

312
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,880
Let's just tell them what we did!

313
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:49,260
Let's call it the textbook's ending,
or something like that!

314
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:50,220
Whatever you like.

315
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:51,620
Here we go!

316
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:53,060
Go ahead.

317
00:16:53,540 --> 00:16:56,280
Where did you make Nobunaga disappear to?

318
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,440
Well, after that,
I don't know where he went.

319
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:01,200
But well, so there was a gap
in history after all, right?

320
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:02,560
Then this time for sure.

321
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:03,140
Yeah!

322
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:08,140
Over one mountain, past the bookshelf,
off to Osaka Castle, go!

323
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:24,020
We did it, Lord Ryotsu!

324
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:26,260
Now I'm rich too!

325
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:29,860
Make way for the lord's arrival!

326
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:35,140
Lord Ryotsu, Lord Honda,
please raise your heads.

327
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:40,100
Hideyoshi, you've become quite the man!

328
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:42,900
No, it's all thanks to you two.

329
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,840
You haven't forgotten our promise, have you?

330
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:46,700
Of course, I haven't forgotten.

331
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:58,640
Oban and koban coins, piling up by the heap!

332
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:00,920
Whoa, what's that?

333
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:04,120
Ow

334
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:07,560
Your fun ends there!

335
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:08,800
Ryotsu!

336
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,840
Senpai!

337
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:11,220
That's cruel, Ryo-san!

338
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,180
Shotgun!

339
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:13,860
You lot!

340
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:20,580
Ryotsu Kankichi! Trying to change the
past just to make easy money is outrageous!

341
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:21,620
Therefore, you!

342
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:24,000
I won't stand for talk of a hell tour!

343
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:25,200
Hey!

344
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:26,820
Whoa!

345
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,160
Get off!

346
00:18:32,420 --> 00:18:33,160
It's a nightmare!

347
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:37,340
I'll have you cast adrift to someplace
even more terrifying than a tour of hell!

348
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:41,480
Shittsuiyā makōē, Hondaratta koē!

349
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:42,660
Pihoryā!

350
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:51,180
Where could be more
terrifying than hell, anyway?

351
00:18:59,220 --> 00:19:00,840
Help me, help me!

352
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,560
You were in a time like this?

353
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,800
Monkey, this is your fault!
It's all your fault!

354
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:08,320
Isn't this too realistic to be a dream?

355
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:30,740
Noooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

356
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:34,900
If it happens again, waking up is nice.

357
00:19:35,620 --> 00:19:39,380
Even boring stories,

358
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:44,100
heat up my whole body.

359
00:19:44,370 --> 00:19:50,780
But I want to see my friends.

360
00:19:51,050 --> 00:19:54,400
I surely want to be loved.

361
00:19:54,400 --> 00:20:00,160
Just enough beer to make fun of me,

362
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:05,900
feeling like we're melting into each other.

363
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:09,900
I surely want to confide.

364
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:15,540
For some reason, only love makes me timid.

365
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:19,100
Days that repeat themselves,
that's all over now.

366
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:23,220
Don't hide everything.

367
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:29,000
I want to be loved someday

368
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:34,380
the child I never let out of the house

369
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:39,920
hug me tight

370
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:44,000
I want to properly confess

371
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:49,940
always cheerful, but really

372
00:20:49,940 --> 00:20:57,560
I'm so in love with you
that I can hear your lies

373
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:13,880
Today I have some sad news for all of you

374
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,420
That Ryotsu

375
00:21:15,420 --> 00:21:17,320
That Ryotsu

376
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:19,440
That Ryotsu

377
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:24,920
is going and starring in a movie,
of all things

378
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:29,060
This is the Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box,
Katsushika Ward

379
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:32,720
The Movie, grand premiere at New Year's 2000

380
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:34,420
I haven't heard a thing about this!

